/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/ARCH-ALTERNATIVES-2026-09-09.md:13:Regret is the anchor-local exact nominal score gap to the best candidate in the same panel, in the corpus's normalized units. Realised pooled EE is the ratio of summed realised bits to summed realised joules after replaying each selected configuration through the unchanged keyed-fading evaluator. The selected-size entries are `coalition size:anchor count`.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/ARCH-ALTERNATIVES-2026-09-09.md:76:The authenticated corpus has 11,924 rows at 180 anchors, with size histogram `{'2': 6921, '3': 4691, '4': 270, '5': 36, '6': 6}` and family-index digest `b8f55dc15e91155a32aa706a4908aff3bf6ee281565f9ca0644d76679e7da047`. Five deterministic SHA-256 folds hold out complete anchors; each row is scored once by a model that saw no row from that anchor. Fold counts are `[(145, 35), (144, 36), (138, 42), (143, 37), (150, 30)]`.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/ARCH-ALTERNATIVES-2026-09-09.md:78:The common singleton component is a production-shaped 8-unit ReLU score-difference head trained on the exact singleton receipts. The baseline interaction is `sum h(i,j)`, where `h` is trained on exact atomic pair receipts and cannot represent a nonzero higher-order residual. Alternative A is the resource formula above. Alternative B is a 96/48-unit RankNet score trained only on ordered pairs from the same training anchor; it never sees cross-anchor pairs. All feature scaling and the rank score's secondary affine calibration are fit on training folds only.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/ARCH-ALTERNATIVES-2026-09-09.md:84:R-squared is computed after demeaning exact targets and predictions within each held-out anchor × coalition-size cell. It therefore cannot be inflated by between-anchor level differences. Ranker scores receive one training-only positive scale per fold; ranking itself is unchanged.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-curve-ws/V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:85:The C2 tie-break diagnostic is the fraction of non-incumbent (user, action) candidates whose C2 head score is exactly equal to the incumbent's under the FULL arm, i.e. C2 cannot discriminate the move and the ranking falls through to C1 plus the stable configuration-ID tie-break. `c2_tie_frequency` is the fraction of anchor-seed decisions with any such tie; `c2_tie_pair_fraction_mean` is the mean per-decision tie fraction. See DEFECTS.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-curve-ws/V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:90:2. Oracle factor-score removal: not run; stage-4 physics receipts remain separate.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-curve-ws/V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:112:- **D-MIN-4 (internal inconsistency). `V_CA` is large and negative while `FULL` pooled EE is the highest of all arms.** Net `V_CA` is -1.365e11 bit-equivalents (bits -1.222e10, -eta*energy -3.373e10, Phi -9.054e10) against the additive selector, yet `FULL` pooled EE (3.425e7) exceeds `DROP_C3` (2.352e7), `S0` (1.759e7) and `BASELINE` (1.699e7). Either the `V_CA` reference (the additive selector) or the pooled-EE aggregation is not measuring what the schema intends. **This must be resolved before any V_CA number is reported at scale.**
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-curve-ws/V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:113:- **D-MIN-5 (now measured, previously zero-by-construction). C2 tie frequency.** The build-3 code had no C2 tie-break and the field was hard-coded `False`. This pilot implemented the smallest schema-satisfying measurement: the fraction of non-incumbent (user, action) candidates whose FULL-arm C2 head score exactly equals the incumbent's. Measured value: **0.0** on both catalogue anchors (`c2_tie_frequency` 0.0, `c2_tie_pair_fraction_mean` 0.0). The C2 head discriminates every candidate; the zero is now an observation rather than an artefact, but it is still a proxy for head indiscriminability, not for a build-3 tie-break code path.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-curve-ws/V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:129:- Build 3 has no explicit C2 tie-break implementation. Stable total score then configuration ID is used. The C2 tie statistic reported here was implemented by this pilot as the smallest schema-satisfying measurement (exact C2-score equality against the incumbent); it measures head indiscriminability, not a build-3 tie-break code path.
